Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 10 48 CLINICAL DATA  66 year old with new nipple inversion with small mass at 12 o clock                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   RIGHT MASS    BIOPSY  INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  CRIBRIFORM AND NEUROENDOCRINE TYPES  PRESENT IN THREE OF FOUR BIOPSY FRAGMENTS AND PRESENT LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM SEVERAL INKED SURFACES   SEE NOTE   NOTE  Definite stromal  lymphatic and blood vascular invasion is not seen  Immunoperoxidase stain for chromogranin is focally positive  Dr  Koerner has reviewed this case and agrees with the interpretation  Ref  Maluf  H and Koerner  F  1994  Carcinomas of the breast with endocrine differentiation  a review  Virchows Archiv 425  REMOVED_DATE  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 16 18                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The in situ tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The in situ tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Invasive carcinoma is not present in the sections stained for hormone receptor proteins  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 21 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast mass  are four fragments of breast tissue  ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest diameter  Cautery artifact is seen on the surface of the largest fragment which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal focally yellow and focally white unremarkable breast parenchyma  entirely in cassettes A through I  The next largest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal focally pink and focally white unremarkable breast tissue  entirely in cassettes J and K  The next fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is inked and sectioned to reveal mostly unremarkable fatty breast parenchyma  Specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette L  The smallest fragment measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is covered by a red smooth lining  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal focally red and focally white tissue  entirely submitted in cassette M  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT MASS   BIOPSY  report_end , 1.
