Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 36 CLINICAL DATA  Increasing mass REMOVED_DATE cm   phyllodes                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  MULTIPLE ADJACENT FOCI  THE LARGEST NODULE IS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON THE GROSS SPECIMEN  A SECOND NODULE IS REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION AS MEASURED ON THE GROSS SPECIMEN  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA IS PRESENT AT MULTIPLE MARGINS OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE   NOTE  No definite intraductal component is identified  Definite blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnoses are confirmed  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  09 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 22                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 13 39 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of breast tissue  Inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well defined  white to focally yellow  firm  gritty nodule  abutting the resection margin in multiple points  Other scattered well defined firm nodules  the largest REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter  abutting the resection margin are also identified  Representative sections of the large nodule are frozen as FX 1  representative section of the 1 cm nodule is frozen as FX 2  Frozen tissue saved frozen for ER PR and IP if necessary  Representative sections of larger tumor in A through C  smaller tumor submitted in D  Additional suspicious breast tissue in E through G  Resident  EDWIN S  MONUKI  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST MASS   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  RIGHT BREAST MASS   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST MASS  report_end , 1.
