Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status  Signed Type  Surgical Pathology Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE      ADDENDUM MESSAGE         ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION     This report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing additional diagnostic information  Please refer to the ADDENDUM REPORT section below for this information  The original diagnosis is unchanged  ADDENDUM REPORT Addendum  1 Entered  REMOVED_DATE  0838 Fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu performed at Mayo Medical Laboratories on block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  reveals the following results for the infiltrating carcinoma  The specimen showed NO evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu gene amplification  Addeundum Signed Electronically Signed KOELLIKER DANIEL D  M D  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS  A  Left breast  lateral   excision  Invasive ductal carcinoma  poorly differentiated  see note   Ductal carcinoma in situ  intermediate grade  2 3   solid type  with focal necrosis and microcalcifications  Fibrocystic changes with microcalcifications  B  Left breast  subareolar   excision  Epidermoid cyst with acute inflammation  granulation tissue and surrounding chronic inflammation and fibroplasia consistent with abscess formation  Surrounding breast tissue with unremarkable ducts  NOTE  In the left lateral excision  specimen A   the invasive tumor is REMOVED_DATE cm  in size and is present at the inked margin focally and is less than REMOVED_DATE  cm  from the margin in multiple foci  No lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen  Immunohistochemical stains performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following for the invasive carcinoma  Estrogen receptor  POSITIVE Progesterone receptor  POSITIVE Her2 neu  c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   2  staining  Further evaluation by fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  method will be performed and results reported in an addendum to follow  Ductal carcinoma in situ is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm  in size and is present within and adjacent to the invasive carcinoma and is less than REMOVED_DATE cm  from the margin in multiple foci  Final Diagnosis by  Daniel D  Koelliker  M D  Clinical diagnosis   history  Two nodules of left breast Tissue Designation  A Breast  excision with margins   left lateral B Breast  excision with margins   left subareolar Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in two containers  Specimen A labeled  left breast lateral  consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue  which is inked and sectioned revealing a firm  white tan tissue  centrally  It is entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  2 agg  all  Specimen B labeled  left subareolar biopsy  consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  portion of primarily rubbery  white tan fibrous tissue with a small amount of inner mixed adipose tissue  The specimen contains a localizing wire  It is inked  cross sectioned and entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  4 agg  all  Dictated by  DDK____ signature on file ____MICHAEL J  ROSS  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final  ____ signature on file ____DANIEL D  KOELLIKER  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 0.
