deep margins consists of a smooth fascial plane  In the superior midline area of the deep margin  there is a stitch marking previous resection with DCIS  Cut sections reveal a couple of firm regions  2 x 2 x 1 cm  3 x 2 x 1 cm   superior to the nipple at the midline  and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from skin and REMOVED_DATE cm from deep margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable and consists of 60  fibrous tissue and 40  adipose tissue  In the region of the stitch  in the deep margin  there is a biopsy cavity  1 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm  with some clotted blood  There are fourteen  14  tan lymph nodes in the axillary tail  the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter  Micro REMOVED_DATE  left breast  deep margin at area with stitch  1 frag each  ESS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  left breast  firm region  1 to 2 frags each  RSS  Micro 8   left breast  skin with scar  1 frag  RSS  Micro 9   left breast  upper outer quadrant  1 frag  RSS  Micro 10   left breast  upper inner quadrant  1 frag  RSS  Micro 11   left breast  lower outer quadrant  1 frag  RSS  Micro 12   left breast  lower inner quadrant  1 frag  RSS  Micro 13   left breast  nipple  1 frag  RSS  Micro REMOVED_DATE  left breast  lymph nodes  4 to 5 per cassette  14 frags  ESS  Part  2   left axillary contents  partial sampling  consists of one  1  lymph node and  0 6 cm   and fragments of fibroadipose tissue  2 0 cm in aggregae   Entire specimen is submitted  Micro 17   left axillary contents  partial sampling 1 lymph node  2 frags  ESS  Micro 18   left axillary contents  partial sampling  adipose tissue  multiple frags  ESS  Part  3   right breast tissue   consists of multiple fragments of unoriented fibroadipose tissue and skin measuring in aggregate 9 x 8 x 2 cm  There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive cancer  Representative sections are submitted  Micro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue  1 to 2 frags each  RSS  Reports to  RANDALL  SHELDON M D  SPECIMEN TYPE  BREAST MASTECTOMY 