Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  29 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  29 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 18 03 CLINICAL DATA  54 year old with 8 mm  hypoechoic mass at REMOVED_DATE o clock in the left breast  Six core biopsies with 14 gauge needle                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE BIOPSY  LYMPHOID INFILTRATE WITH REACTIVE FOLLICLES AND PLASMA CELLS  NOTE  The infiltrate is chronic and accompanied by fibrosis  No breast epithelium is identified with certainty  and granulomas are not seen  The differential diagnosis includes a reactive or idiopathic process  lymphocytic or plasma cell mastitis  healing infection or injury  etc   and low grade lymphoma  Immunoperoxidase stains show a mixture of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  B cells in follicles and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  5  43  T cells in the microfollicular region  Plasma cells are polyclonal  kappa  and lambda    The B cells are negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and cyclin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  These results tend to favor a reactive process and to exclude mantle cell and small lymphocytic lymphoma  Marginal zone MALT lymphoma cannot be definitely excluded  but the lack of an extrafollicular B cell proliferation argues against it  This case was discussed with Dr  Alan Pineda on REMOVED_DATE  and further work up may be possible if clinically indicated  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 17 23 Consulting Pathologist s   Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 6 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm which are submitted in toto as