Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Corrected Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 14 16 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Revised on 15 AUG 96 at 08 40                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  APOCRINE CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA WITH APOCRINE FEATURES  APOCRINE CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margins of the mastectomy specimen cannot be evaluated  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 22 OF 22 LYMPH NODES  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 07                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 07     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   Five percent of the tumor cells stain for c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  favorable   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 24                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Irene Kuter  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  COLLEGE OF PHYSICIANS and SURGEONS OF COLUMBIA UNIV  PART A  RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  D REMOVED_CASE_ID  Date of Procedure  09 MAY 1983 Slides  5 Blocks  2 PART B  RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  D REMOVED_CASE_ID  Date of Procedure  14 MAY 1983 Slides  14 Blocks  0  report_end , 0.
