Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  18 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 01 CLINICAL DATA  Inflammation recurrence right breast cancer   dermal lymphatic invasion                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  CONSISTENT WITH INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA INVOLVING SUBCUTANEOUS FAT  NO DEFINITE LYMPHATIC INVASION IS SEEN  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  John O Connell  M D  Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 07 21                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with patient s name and unit number  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm skin ellipse with a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm  and three rubbery tan  fatty tissue fragments  REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate  Entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Resident  Jane M  Yang  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   RIGHT BREAST  BIOPSY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA  INFILTRATING ADIPOSE TISSUE O R  Resident  Michael Pins  M D  O R  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Barbara Smith  M D  PART   BREAST  report_end , 0.
