Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 01 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 18 13 CLINICAL DATA  40 y o female with left breast mass    ca                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT  2 O CLOCK   CORE BIOPSY  INVASIVE AND IN SITU DUCTAL CARCINOMA  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 53                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block A   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells show moderate  2   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and no designation as to site  are 8 cores of fibrofatty tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm which are submitted in toto as cassette A and B  Gross Description by  ALAN ALLBEE Resident  ZUOQIN TANG  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Eren D Yeh  M D  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  George Cohen  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT 2 O CLOCK  CORE BIOPSY, 1.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast core needle biopsy Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  DIANNE GEORGIAN SMITH M D  CASE  BS 08 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  Rachel L Rucker Schmidt  M D  Pathologist  James L Connolly  M D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  UPPER OUTER  14 G ULTRAOSUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A CIRCUMSCRIBED PALPABLE REMOVED_DATE CM MASS LYMPH NODE  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  poorly differentiated consistent with breast ductal primary involving a lymph node  NOTE  Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu will be performed and reported in an addendum  CLINICAL DATA  HISTORY  46 year old with saline implant x 5 years  Right breast with enlarged lymph node a separate mass in same breast that is highly suspicious for ca not yet diagnosed  BREAST IMAGING FINDING  1  Right  8 mm lymph node  Palpable and circumscribed  1  Right  upper outer TYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY  1  14G Ultrasound  DIFDX  Hyperplastic node vs  metastatic node  TISSUE SUBMITTED  1  14G Ultrasound   Brown GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  in one part  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  brown cassette   and consists of multiple yellow white focally hemorrhagic irregular fibrofatty tissues  aggregating REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm   which are received in an unlabeled brown cassette  The specimens are submitted in toto  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Multi frags  ESS  CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  cp ag By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by James L Connolly M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE  SURGICAL ADDENDUM  Immunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the following results for metastatic carcinoma  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE Progesterone receptor NEGATIVE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu  c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  POSITIVE  3   NOTE  No normal breast epithelium is present to act as an internal control for immunohistochemical stains  External controls for ER and PR react appropriately  Hormone receptor analysis  The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the invasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows  positive  10  of nuclei immunoreactive positive   low   0      10  of nuclei immunoreactive negative 0  of nuclei immunoreactive The lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet been determined  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu analysis  Negative  0   No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Negative  1    Faint weak immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells but only a portion of the membrane is positive  Positive  2   Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in  10  of tumor cells  Positive  3   Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in  30  of tumor cells  Cytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result  External controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity  Some of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational use only  Addendum  1 by Jane E  Brock M B   B S   Ph D   Electronically signed on 4 23 2008 SURGICAL ADDENDUM  FISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit with the following  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Results  EQUIVOCAL  see NOTE  HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  The average of HER 2 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The average centromere 17 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  REFERENCE RANGE  NOT AMPLIFIED HER 2 CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  EQUIVOCAL HER 2 CEP 17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE  AMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID CEP 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  NOTE  There is a notable difference in both the REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu protein overexpression and FISH results between the core needle biopsy of the patient s mass  see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and the core needle biopsy of the lymph node metastasis  The primary tumor shows 2  to 3  protein overexpression by immunohistochemistry  and is not amplified by FISH  ratio REMOVED_DATE 2   REMOVED_DATE    with no polysomy present  However the lymph node metastasis shows 3  overexpression by immunohistochemistry and is equivocal for amplification by FISH  ratio REMOVED_DATE   with an increased number of gene copies  5 6  and polysomy noted  This difference between the primary core and metastasis core results suggests that there is tumor heterogeneity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID neu overexpression in this case  Addendum  2 by Jane E  Brock M B   B S   Ph D   Electronically signed on 6 4 2008  report_end , 1.
