itch designating superior  The specimen has been six inked by the surgeon per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins  posterior black  anterior blue  superior red  inferior green  lateral yellow  medial orange  The inside of the specimen is composed almost entirely of firm tan white fibrous tissue  with almost no areas of adipose tissue  Within the medial aspect of the specimen there is a white nodular area that is softer than the surrounding tissue  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin  REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin  0 2 cm from the anterior margin  REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin  and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin  No hemorrhagic areas or necrotic areas or calcifications or prior cavities are identified  The entire specimen is submitted in slices from medial to lateral  with the first cassette being the medial margin  Micro  1  Slice one  medial and superior margins  1 frag  ESS  Micro  2  Slice two  medical  superior and inferior margins showing nodule  1 frag  ESS  Micro  3 4  Slices three and four with superior  inferior  anterior and posterior margins showing nodular area  2 frags  ESS  Micro  5  Slice five  superior  inferior  anterior  and lateral margins  1 frag  ESS  Micro  6  Slices six and seven showing superior  inferior  and lateral margins  2 frags  ESS  Part two   left breast tissue   consists of multiple fragments of unoriented pink tan  friable soft tissue  the largest measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  and the smallest measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  In aggregate  the sample measures 3 x REMOVED_DATE  x REMOVED_DATE cm  The largest specimen is composed of 80  tan white fibrous tissue and the remainder is composed primarily of adipose tissue  There is a small area of necrosis  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm  Representative sections were submitted  Micro  7 