Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 12 38 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  MYXOID MALIGNANT NEOPLASM  FAVOR MATRIX PRODUCING CARCINOMA  NOTE  Certain features also suggest myoepithelial differentiation  Estrogen and progesterone receptor stains will be performed  and the results reported in an addendum  Diagnosis by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 06 Consulting Pathologist s   Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                      RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 09 14     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     NOTE  By immunoperoxidase methods  tumor cells stain for keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2 and REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDprotein  faintly for keratin 903  and some tumor cells stain for alpha smooth muscle actin  The findings are consistent with a carcinoma with myoepithelial differentiation  Added by  John H  Eichhorn  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 35 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name and unit number  with no designation as to site  are multiple tan pink soft cores aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  submitted entirely in cassette A  Gross Description by  Joe Serra Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTPATIENT  OFF P CLINIC  REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  Priscilla Slanetz  M D  Jaime L Kline  M D  PART   BREAST  LEFT   CORE BIOPSY  report_end , 1.
