Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status  Signed Type  Surgical Pathology Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  DIAGNOSIS  Left breast  localization excision  Ductal carcinoma in situ  intermediate grade  cribriform type with necrosis and microcalcifications  see note   Atypical ductal hyperplasia  Atypical lobular hyperplasia  Fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia and microcalcifications  NOTE  At the lateral aspect of the specimen  there is a focus of intermediate grade ductal carcinoma in situ associated with microcalcifications which is about REMOVED_DATE cm  in size and is less than REMOVED_DATE cm  from the superior margin and less than REMOVED_DATE cm  from the inferior margin  Microcalcifications are also present in multiple foci associated with fibrocystic changes and ductal hyperplasia  Final Diagnosis by  Daniel D  Koelliker  M D  Clinical diagnosis   history  Left breast calcium  prior history of right breast carcinoma Tissue Designation  Breast  excision with margins   left Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  left breast mass  long lateral  short superior  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  cm  portion of fibroadipose tissue containing a localizing wire  accompanied by a specimen x ray and marked with two orienting sutures  The margins throughout are inked black  At one end of the specimen  where the wire enters the specimen  there is a long suture oriented as lateral and in the mid portion of one side of the specimen  there is a short suture oriented as superior of the left breast  The superior surface is double inked blue  The deep aspect is double inked red  The specimen is cross sectioned from lateral towards medial revealing mostly rubbery  white tan fibrous tissue  The entire specimen is submitted sequentially beginning at the lateral aspect toward the medial aspect in REMOVED_DATE  5 agg  all  Dictated by  DDK____ signature on file ____RICHARD SAMPSON  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final  ____ signature on file ____DANIEL D  KOELLIKER  M D  REMOVED_DATE   Final   report_end , 0.
