Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ACCESSIONED ON  25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14 40 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast mass  Renal transplant patient                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT S REMOVED_CASE_ID 02   NEEDLE BIOPSY  HIGH GRADE B CELL LYMPHOMA  POST TRANSPLANT LYMPHOPROLIFERATIVE DISORDER  MONOMORPHIC   SEE NOTE   NOTE  There is a diffuse infiltrate of medium sized to large lymphoid cells within the breast  Submitted immunoperoxidase stains show that the tumor cells are positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  pan leukocyte  and negative for cytokeratin  Stains performed here show that the cells are positive for B cell antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and negative for T cell antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and myeloperoxidase  Ki67  proliferation  fraction is  95   Because of the medium sized cells and high proliferation fraction  the differential diagnosis includes Burkitt s lymphoma as well as diffuse large B cell lymphoma  Additional stains  including in situ hybridization for EBV  are in progress and will be reported separately  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  29 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 15 29                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOPEROXIDASE STAINS ON PARAFFIN SECTIONS  With antibody to B lineage antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID there is staining of most cells in a diffuse pattern  The B cells are positive for antibody to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and Bcl 6 and negative for Bcl 2  With antibody to T lineage associated antigen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID there is staining of rare small cells  The cells are also positive for Ki67  approximately 100    The cells are negative for myeloperoxidase  Together with the morphologic features on routine sections  these results confirm the diagnosis of B cell lymphoma  high grade and support the diagnosis of atypical Burkitt s lymphoma  See note  NOTE  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13 39     ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION Addendum     In situ hybridization  ISH  performed on a paraffin embedded section reveals POSITIVE STAINING of MANY TUMOR cells with an oligonucleotide probe specific for EBV encoded RNA  EBER   The findings are consistent with a post transplantation lymphoma  Added by  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  Signed On  08 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 17 19                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Francis Leo Delmonico  M D  Judith Ann Ferry  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  BEVERLY HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Anne Moran  M D  WENTWORTH DOUGLASS HOSPITAL 789 CENTRAL AVENUE DOVER  NH REMOVED_DATE  2132 PART   BREAST  RIGHT  S REMOVED_CASE_ID 02  BIOPSY Date of Procedure  23 OCT 2002 Slides  6 Blocks  1, 0.
