Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Skin biopsy  other than cyst tag debrid repair Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  KARL H BREUING M D  CASE  BS 07 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME Resident  Eric C Huang  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Hejin P Hahn  M D   Ph D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  SPECIMEN LABELLED  TISSUE FROM LEFT BREAST    BUT SPECIMEN DESIGNATED SKIN FROM RIGHT CHEEK BY SURGEON  SEE NOTE   Skin with scar and subcutaneous tissue with abscess and granuloma formation and foreign body giant cell reaction  See NOTE  MSS and AFB stains are negative for fungal and acid fast organisms  respectively  NOTE  Although the pathology requisition form lists the specimen as left breast tissue and the procedure as exploration and closure of left breast wound  according to the surgeon the specimen is actually an excision of a tethered right cheek face scar  CLINICAL DATA  Clinical History  Non healing wound left breast  Operation  Suture removal  exploration and closure left breast  Operative Findings  None given  Clinical Diagnosis  Non healing wound left breast  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  Tissue from left breast  GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  tissue from left breast   and consists of an irregular tan granular unoriented skin  2 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm  excised to depth of REMOVED_DATE cm   The epithelial surface exhibits a peripheral granular ulcerated brown lesion  0 3 x 0 3 cm  REMOVED_DATE from the closest radial margin  The specimen is inked and sectioned to exhibit an yellow tan focally fibrotic cut surface with no masses or lesions identified  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Specimen serially sectioned  with epithelial lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  multi frags total  ESS  CASE NUMBER  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lmc ag By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Final Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 3 5 2007  report_end , 0.
Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Amend Addenda Type  Surgical Pathology Specimen Type  Breast  mastectomy w o regional lymph nodes Procedure Date  REMOVED_DATE  Ordering Provider  DIANE C LOCKHART M D  CASE  BS 06 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PATIENT  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME            Addended Report             Resident  Michael H Roh  M D   Ph D  Pathologist  Alessandra F Nascimento  M D  PATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS  RIGHT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  No residual in situ or invasive carcinoma present  Scarring  fibrosis and foreign body giant cell reaction consistent with biopsy site changes  Skin with scarring  LEFT BREAST  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  METASTATIC CARCINOMA  3 5 cm  to one  1  of sixteen  16  axillary lymph nodes  see NOTE   Tumor shows extensive necrosis  Small foci of extracapsular extension are identified  Immunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining profile in tumor cells  Positive   ER  PR  low   1  of cells   Her2 neu  weak  patchy  The immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis  Breast with one intraparenchymal lymph node showing fibrosis and scarring consistent with prior biopsy site  No in situ or invasive carcinoma identified in breast parenchyma  Skeletal muscle present  Skin with no significant pathologic change  NOTE  The tumor in the current specimen  left axillary lymph node  is histologically slightly different from this patient s contralateral primary breast carcinoma diagnosed in 2000 in the right breast  BWH ref REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  8 14 2000   The current neoplasm shows some columnar changes and scattered pleomorphic cells  These differences could probably be attributed to prior treatment  In addition  the current tumor is weakly positive for Her2 neu and very focally positive for PR  the contralateral primary was ER and PR positive  and Her2 neu negative   The latter finding is likely related to aromatase inhibitor therapy  The weak and patchy positivity for Her2 neu is of uncertain significance and the paraffin block will be submitted for fluorescence in situ hybridization  FISH  for analysis of amplification of the gene  The results of this study will be reported in an addendum  The left mastectomy specimen has been thoroughly examined in an attempt to identify a possible tiny left breast carcinoma but no tumor mass was identified in the breast parenchyma  Although there are some morphologic and immunophenotypic differences between the current neoplasm and the one diagnosed in 2000  right breast   spread from the contralateral primary cannot be excluded  Selected slides of this case were reviewed by Dr  Susan Lester  Breast Pathology Service  who concurs  CLINICAL DATA  History  55 year old woman with R invasive ductal CA treated 2000 with BCT XRT chemo tx presented with mass in left axilla  Core bx L ax mass and imaging c w metastatic breast disease  occult disease in left breast suspected  Operation  L MRM  R simple prophylactic mastectomy  Clinical Diagnosis  Left occult breast CA  TISSUE SUBMITTED  A 1  right breast  suture   tail of spence   B 2  left breast  suture on axillary tail   GROSS DESCRIPTION  The specimen is received fresh  in two parts  each labeled with the patients name and unit number  Part A  labeled   1   right breast  suture   tail of spence    consists of a right simple mastectomy specimen weighing 723 grams  20 5 x 16 x REMOVED_DATE cm   including a skin ellipse  17 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm   which contains a nipple  3 5 x REMOVED_DATE  cm   There is a 3 cm linear scar that is present at the inferior lateral aspect of the nipple  at a distance of 1 cm from the areola   The tail of spence is marked by a suture per surgeon and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  The deep aspect of the specimen consists of a smooth and glistening fascial plane with no skeletal muscle grossly evident  This deep surface is inked blue  Serial sectioning of the specimen reveals an area of granular fibrous tissue  3 0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  within the breast parenchyma that is located 1 cm to the nearest inked deep margin  This area corresponds to and is deep to the scar on the skin ellipse  The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of over 90  adipose tissue with intervening white fibrous strands  No other lesions are identified  The tail of spence is examined for lymph nodes and none are identified  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  granular area including skin with scar  1 frag per cassette  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  granular area with respect to deep margin  3 frags total  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  remainder of granular area  2 frags total  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  upper outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lower outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  upper inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lower inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  nipple  1 frag  RSS  Part B  labeled   2   left breast suture on axillary tail   consists of a left modified radical mastectomy specimen  1 2 kilograms  30 x 20 x 5 cm   including an axillary tail  12 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  marked by suture per surgeon and a skin ellipse  22 x REMOVED_DATE cm  that includes a nipple  4 0 x REMOVED_DATE cm   The deep aspect of the specimen consists of a smooth and glistening fascial plane  inked blue  with no skeletal muscle grossly evident  Within the axillary tail there is a prominent enlarged lymph node  3 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  that is grossly involved by firm white tissue interspersed with tan brown areas  This node is well encapsulated  Examination of the breast parenchyma reveals no grossly apparent lesions  in fact  over 95  of the breast parenchyma is composed of adipose tissue with scarce intervening tan white fibrous tissue strands  There is a single intramammary lymph node at the 3 o clock position marked by a clip consistent with a previously biopsied node  This node measures approximately 0 8 cm in greatest dimension  Examination of the axillary tail tissue reveals an additional lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  This node displays fatty replacement  Fourteen additional nodes are identified  This gross specimen was reviewed with Dr  Lester  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  largest lymph node and surrounding fibroadipose tissue  1 frag per cassette  RSS  approximately 40  of this node is submitted for histologic evaluation   Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  second largest lymph node with fatty replacement  2 frags total  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  bisected lymph node  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  bisected lymph node  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  bisected lymph node  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  three lymph nodes  3 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  four lymph nodes  4 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  two lymph nodes  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  two lymph nodes  2 frags  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  area surrounding clip including previously biopsied intramammary node  3 frags total  ESS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  upper outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lower outer quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  upper inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  lower inner quadrant  2 frags  RSS  Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  nipple  1 frag  RSS  ROH lp By his her signature below  the senior physician certifies that he she personally conducted a microscopic examination   gross only  exam if so stated  of the described specimen s  and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis es  related thereto  Resident Review by Michael H Roh M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Prelim Dx Release by Michael H Roh M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  No Action   Prelim Sent by Alessandra F Nascimento M D   on REMOVED_DATE  Final Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M D   Electronically signed on 1 17 2006 Surgical Addendum   1 24 06  FISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER 2 DNA Probe Kit with the following results  block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Result  NOT AMPLIFIED The Her 2 cen 17 ratio   REMOVED_DATE  The average of Her 2 neu copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The average of cen 17 copies per cell  REMOVED_DATE  The cutoff point for assessing HER 2 neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE  Addendum by Andrea L Richardson M D   Ph D   on REMOVED_DATE  Addendum  1 by Andrea L Richardson M D   Ph D   Electronically signed on 1 24 2006  report_end , 0.
