Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  CorrectedType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ACCESSIONED ON  09 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 13 19 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided      REVISED REPORT     Reason for Revision  ADDITIONAL TISSUE RECEIVED Revised by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Revised on 23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 06                                                                                     FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   1  Infiltrating ductal carcinoma  65    REMOVED_DATE cm moderately differentiated  Grade II III   focally extending to an inked  cauterized surface  with focal pagetoid spread and cancerization of lobules  See Note   2  Intraductal carcinoma  35    cribriform and solid type  focally present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from an inked surface  3  Atypical intraductal hyperplasia  and intraductal hyperplasia  multifocal  4  Fibrocystic changes  NOTE  Blood vascular and lymphatic invasion is not see  Calcifications are associated with the intraductal carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 20                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 12 41                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Simon Powell  M D  Michael Grossbard  M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  WOMEN AND INFANTS HOSPITAL OF RHODE ISLAND OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  Margaret M  Steinhoff  M D  DEPT  OF PATH WOMEN and INFANTS  HOSPITAL 101 DUDLEY STREET PROVIDENCE  RI REMOVED_DATE  274 1100 PART   RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Date of Procedure  21 OCT 1994 Slides  10 Blocks  10  report_end , 0.
