Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  02 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 20 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  INFILTRATING CARCINOMA EXHIBITING BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  100   EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 58                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN  THE TUMOR CELLS STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN  SEE NOTE  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  16 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13 47 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab and labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast tissue which is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan pink firm  stellate mass extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm to the inked resection margin  A representative section is frozen and saved frozen  The rest of the specimen submitted in A through J  Resident  STEPHEN LAU  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1   LEFT BREAST   INFILTRATING CARCINOMA  SUGGESTIVE OF INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  O R  Resident  FANG FANG  MD  PhD O R  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  BIOPSY  report_end , 0.
