Accession Number  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 13 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   DUCTAL CARCINOMA  FOCALLY INFILTRATING  WELL DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  TUBULAR   C 60   AND IN SITU  C 40   MULTIFOCAL  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Both infiltrative and in situ carcinoma components are multifocal  Invasive carcinoma focally extends very close to  less than 1 mm from  an inked margin  and ductal carcinoma in situ focally extends to within a fraction of a mm of a margin  Neither blood vessel nor lymphatic invasion is identified  Diagnosis by  Ben Zion Pilch  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 31                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 10 31 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast biopsy specimen with localizing wire in place and accompanying x ray  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal white rubbery tissue intermixed with fat yellow tissue  and a REMOVED_DATE cm diameter firm white nodule  REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest inked margin  All submitted in cassette A through G  nodule in cassette A   Resident  Suzanne B  Keel  M D      INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  LEFT BREAST   AN REMOVED_DATE CM SUSPICIOUS NODULE  TOO SMALL TO FREEZE  EXPLAINED TO SURGEON  AWAIT PERMANENTS  O R  Resident  Karen C  Deering  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Leslie Wayne Ottinger  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST  report_end , 1.
