ematopoiesis with scattered small lymphocytes  No lymphoma seen   Clinical  67 year old female with NHL  large cell  left breast   CLINICAL DATA  History  67 year old female with newly diagnosed lymphoma of the left breast diagnosed REMOVED_DATE    large cell    high grade  Currently being staged  no additional disease discerned but left breast mass is gallium negative suggesting lower grade disease  On no treatment  Clinical Diagnosis  Rule out lymphoma involvement  TISSUE SUBMITTED  Consult slides  GROSS DESCRIPTION  by JORGENSEN JEFFREY LEE M D  PH D  Received from Faulkner Hospital are four glass slides labelled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabelled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PanT REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID panB  and  LCA REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   which correspond to a H E and immunostains from a left breast biopsy performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient s name and number  Received from South Shore Hospital  S  Weymouth MA are fifteen glass slides labelled  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  and sublabelled  Fe   3    Retic   3    PAS   2  and two H E stains as well as four Wright Giemsa and one iron stained aspirate that correspond to a bone marrow biopsy and aspirate performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient s name and number  Reports to  SPECIMEN TYPE  OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT   HEME COMPREHENSIVE  report_end , 0.
